(text "REVIEW ONLY / OPAQUE COTS USAGE\nGomSpace A/S / NanoPower P80 (configuration 1)\nProduct ID: gomspace-p80-config1\nPart number: NanoPower P80, configuration 1 (ordering designation, numeric P/N not stated)\nRevision: catalog-record-1; product hardware revision not stated\nAllocated roles: conditioning, distribution, processor. One physical usage record. Quantity: 1.\nAccounting boundary: One complete configuration-1 assembly including PMU, ACU, PDU, enclosure and\ninternal electronics. All conditioning/distribution/processor allocations reference this same\nphysical usage and contribute its 0.3608 kg once. BP8 battery, external harness, mating connectors\nand spacecraft mounting are separate.\nSupported catalog configurations (none is automatically chosen):\nConfiguration 1 only: 1×PMU, 1×ACU, 1×PDU in enclosure. ACU has 12 PV inputs in two banks of six\nMPPT boost converters.\nPDU channel-to-regulator assignments are factory hardware configuration. Regulated and raw-battery\noutputs coexist. Other P80 stack configurations have different mass/envelopes and are outside this\nrecord.\nSources (exact URLs and document revisions also in manifest.json):\nNanoPower P80 Datasheet / DS 1047423, revision 2.3.0, 2024-09-24\nhttps://gomspace.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Data-Sheet-NanoPower-P80.pdf\nLocation: Printed pp. 1–23 (PDF pp. 8–30). Tables 1.1–1.2 pp. 5–6. Table 2.2 pp. 7–8. Table 4.1 p.\n22.. Retrieved: 2026-10-17\nCatalog caveats:\nCanonical level board represents a multi-board enclosed assembly here, not a single PCB.\nConfiguration 1 must remain fixed for these physical values.\nThe datasheet explicitly excludes BP8 from the P80 EPS boundary (printed p. 2). Do not add a battery\nrole or battery capacity to P80.\n25 V PV input maximum is distinct from the additional Voc < max(VBAT) condition. No\nminimum/startup/tracking envelope or aggregate input-power limit is inferred.\nRegulator efficiency is supplied as typical curves versus load and battery voltage, not one\nguaranteed system efficiency. No scalar is adopted.\nMCUs and watchdogs are explicit. MCU model, memory, compute headroom and firmware release/timing\nevidence are missing. No independent software role is claimed." (at 25.4 59.69 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left)) (uuid 33e8d62f-7e2f-47c2-8bba-8bcdd2dda6e0))
